# Fix Table Width in Print View

When the user asks to fix table width in print view (or similar), apply this solution:

## 1. Wrap the table in a full-bleed container

Add a wrapper class (e.g. `sales-orders-table-wrap`) around the element containing the table:
```html
<div class="col-lg-12 sales-orders-table-wrap">
    <div class="card">
        ...
        <div class="table-responsive">
            <table id="salesOrdersTable" class="table ...">
```

## 2. Add print CSS (inside @media print)

```css
@page { margin: 8mm; size: auto; }

/* Table full width - full-bleed + explicit column widths */
.sales-orders-table-wrap {
    width: 100vw !important; max-width: 100vw !important;
    position: relative !important; left: 50% !important; margin-left: -50vw !important;
    padding-left: 4px !important; padding-right: 4px !important;
    box-sizing: border-box !important;
}
.sales-orders-table-wrap .card { width: 100% !important; max-width: none !important; }
.sales-orders-table-wrap .card-body { padding: 4px !important; width: 100% !important; }
.sales-orders-table-wrap .table-responsive {
    width: 100% !important; max-width: none !important; overflow: visible !important;
}
#salesOrdersTable {
    width: 100% !important; min-width: 100% !important; max-width: 100% !important;
    table-layout: fixed !important; box-sizing: border-box !important;
}
#salesOrdersTable th, #salesOrdersTable td {
    border: 1px solid #dee2e6 !important; box-sizing: border-box !important;
}
/* Explicit column widths - adjust nth-child and % per table (must total 100%) */
#salesOrdersTable th:nth-child(1), #salesOrdersTable td:nth-child(1) { width: 5% !important; }
#salesOrdersTable th:nth-child(2), #salesOrdersTable td:nth-child(2) { width: 10% !important; }
/* ... continue for each column ... */
```

## 3. Adjust column widths per table

Use `th:nth-child(n)` and `td:nth-child(n)` with percentage widths that sum to 100%. Match the table ID in the CSS to the table's `id` attribute.

## Key points

- **Full-bleed trick**: `left: 50%; margin-left: -50vw` makes the wrapper span full viewport width.
- **table-layout: fixed** + explicit column widths ensure columns stretch to fill the table.
- **@page { margin: 8mm }** reduces default print margins.
- Reuse the same pattern for any report/ledger table needing full-width print.
